{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1522184-exorcist-and-exorcisms","id":1522184,"title":"Exorcist and exorcisms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-06T15:19:23-07:00","id":1522184,"title":"Exorcist and exorcisms","content":"Player I have want to do a character that comes from a family of exorcists that work for the church.it looks like they are going to have to split their focus between mind, spirit and death. I'm trying to see if there is a simpler way and the path that would make this easier for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3647-eric-ericson","name":"Eric Ericson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T15:36:23-07:00","id":1522186,"title":"","content":"Taking a legacy which has one of those as a ruling Arcanum and a path with another at least gives two of the three Arcana are ruling.<br /> <br /> So a Mastigos with a Death Primary legacy could start with Mind 2, Space 1, Death 2, Spirit 1 (but would need Gnosis 2 to get the first legacy attainment).<br /> <br /> Legacy Oblations and attainments based on then family's exorcism-related practices could be interesting (assuming they are actual effective exorcists, not frauds).<br /> <br /> Focusing on one of the three Arcana seems to have more utility, but if that is what they want... Challenging them with other invisible entities, like abbysal entites in some other twilight, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T15:56:37-07:00","id":1522187,"title":"","content":"Practically, Mind should be of lower priority as there aren\u2019t much ephemeral entities aligned with Mind to exorcise on the physical world. So a Thyrsus or Moros who double-majors in Spirit &amp; Death, that picks up Mind only later.<br /> <br /> You as the ST can also arbitrarily skew the encounters towards spirits or ghosts, making a focus on only one Arcanum feel more useful. If the mages are Thyrsus/Moros this even makes in-universe sense via their Long-Term Nimbuses.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also the half-joke half-serious option of having a burly Obrimos with only 1 dot each in Spirit/Death/Mind for the sensory spells but 3 dots in Prime for Ephemeral Enchantment, who proceedes to bellow HEAVENLY FIRE RECTIFIES YOU as they physically wrestle down ephemerals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T19:47:57-07:00","id":1522199,"title":"","content":"I am very much a fan of Fist Exorcist.<br /> <br /> The metagame-y option is a Moros, with a Spirit-based Legacy. A custom one based around exorcism would be best, but the Lords of the Inanimate would be a good fit for a Moros*, the Gaolers of Ialdabaoth are good for the broad exorcist theme, and the Thrice-Great are general spirit-truckers. They'd all need a 2e update, obviously.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Though their 1e Incarnation was Thyrsus","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T10:07:23-07:00","id":1522223,"title":"","content":"Others have described Legacies, but I think something worth recognising is that there isn't a very direct or highly dedicated path to exorcism for mages because it's probably not going to be a heavy focus for one to do. Possessing entities aren't exactly super common, and mages are made with more diverse applications in mind. A person might come from a family line that possessed Supernatural Merits for exorcism or something, but one of the most organic narrative trajectories for that character is to find that Awakening brings them into a larger world than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T10:49:34-07:00","id":1522225,"title":"","content":"Another good angle is Perfected Metals. Lunargent mirrors for seeing into Twilight and Kassiterum... weapons? I guess? Tools of Perfected Tin, at any rate. Ooo! Kassiterum acupuncture needles!<br /> <br /> Anyway, those would make good exorcism tools, but serve as Path Yantras just as easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T12:05:16-07:00","id":1522226,"title":"","content":"I would say a combination of Prime and Space. Prime should let you have <i>Truesight </i>with an Unveiling, being able to see all layers of Twilight, without knowing which one the being you saw is in. A version of <i>Ward</i> using Prime to distinguish all non-supernatural beings (by focusing on the purview of revelation) would allow them to create a seal against anything that is not mundane. <i>Isolation </i>combined with this aspect could be used as an anti-supernatural repulsion field on a subject. <i>Imbue Room</i> can be used to create sacred locations, imbue items for talismans and <i>Stored Spell</i> for creating charms. Lastly, <i>Sacred Geometry</i>, alongside other ley line and Node manipulating spells could allow them to tend to sacred sites (similar to feng shui).<br /> <br /> Another benefit is that this combination of Arcana allows them to investigate possessions discretely. Space lets them get in and out of secure areas, diminishing the risk of getting caught and allows them to follow emotional trails. Prime lets them detect lies easily, hide their abilities (Nimbus and spells), plus manipulate things in any layer of Twilight.<br /> <br /> I believe all that should build up to a capable exorcist, although I was thinking more of a Taoist theme (using fulu charms, lucky coins and so on), but I believe it could be adapted to a church exorcist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 09-07-2023, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}